  "thumbnail": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1614680376573-df3480f0c6ff?q=80&w=1200&auto=format&fit=crop",
  "keyPoints": {
    "en": [
      "Class advantage doubles damage output (and reduces incoming damage)—always bring a Servant with class advantage against the enemy's primary class for the most impactful single change to team performance.",
      "NP (Noble Phantasm) gauge charges through Brave Chains—a 3-card Brave Chain (three cards of the same Servant in one turn) generates bonus NP gauge and critical stars simultaneously; prioritise Brave Chains over raw damage chains.",
      "Craft Essences (CE) have a higher impact on performance than Servant level in most content—a level 1 SSR Servant with a maxed MLB (Max Limit Break) CE often outperforms a fully levelled 4-star Servant without a matching CE.",
      "The Support list from friends provides free access to high-rarity Servants not in your own roster—always include one friend Support Servant in your frontline for any quest with a difficulty higher than 3 stars.",
      "Gapless NP looping requires specific NP charge values, Mystic Code, and refund math—the most reliable beginner loop uses Arts chains (3 Arts cards) with a support Merlin or Castoria to generate the NP gauge needed for back-to-back NPs."
    ],
    "ja": [
      "クラス相性はダメージ出力を2倍にし（受けるダメージを減らす）、敵の主要クラスに対してクラス相性のあるサーヴァントを必ず連れてくることがチームパフォーマンスへの最も影響力のある単一の変化。",
      "NP（宝具）ゲージはブレイブチェーンでチャージする。1ターンに同じサーヴァントのカードを3枚（ブレイブチェーン）使うとボーナスNPゲージとクリティカルスターが同時に生成される。生のダメージチェーンよりブレイブチェーンを優先する。",
      "礼装（CE）はほとんどのコンテンツでサーヴァントのレベルよりパフォーマンスへの影響が大きい。最大限界突破（MLB）礼装を持つレベル1のSSRサーヴァントは、マッチングする礼装なしの完全レベルの4つ星サーヴァントを上回ることが多い。",
      "フレンドのサポートリストは自分のロースターにない高レアリティサーヴァントへの無料アクセスを提供する。難易度3つ星以上のクエストでは、常にフレンドのサポートサーヴァントをフロントラインに含める。",
      "NPゲージの継続チャージには特定のNPチャージ値、神秘のコード、払い戻しの計算が必要。最も信頼できる初心者ループは、バックトゥバックNPに必要なNPゲージを生成するためにサポートのマーリンまたはカストリアとアーツチェーン（アーツカード3枚）を使用する。"
    ]
  },
  "opening": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Story Mode AP Management",
        "body": "AP (Action Points) regenerates at 1 per minute (1 AP per 5 minutes in standard rate). Use AP exclusively for story quests and main story completion in the first month—avoid farming event nodes until you have completed the first 3 story chapters, as story completion unlocks better farming nodes. The Saint Quartz (premium currency) from story completion provides the most reliable source of gacha currency without real money investment; completing all story chapters to Part 2 provides approximately 800+ Saint Quartz."
      },
      {
        "title": "Early Team Composition",
        "body": "Arash (1-star Archer, free) is the most efficient first-wave clearer in the game—his NP is a self-sacrifice that destroys enemies and charges the backline's NP gauge. Include Arash in all 3-wave farming setups as a wave 1 cleaner. For the second Servant slot, use the highest-rarity friend support available (Merlin, Castoria, Skadi). For the third slot, use your highest-damage Servant of matching class advantage. This 1+1+1 frontline pattern covers 80% of early story quests."
      }
    ]
  },
  "midGame": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Event Participation Priority",
        "body": "Limited Events provide the highest-value items in FGO including event-limited Servants, upgrade materials, and MLB event CEs. During events, prioritise clearing the main event story first (unlocks the highest-value shop currency nodes) then farm the node with the highest drops-per-AP for your current resource priority. Event shop items to buy first: upgrade materials in short supply from your current Servant queue > event Servant ascension materials > extra EXP cards."
      },
      {
        "title": "Skill Upgrade Priority",
        "body": "Skills in FGO range from levels 1–10 and cost progressively more materials. Upgrade the primary attack skill and the NP charge skill to level 10 first on your main damage-dealer—the difference between skill level 1 and 10 is typically 15–30% in the primary effect value. Level the third (utility) skill to level 6 only, which provides 80% of the level-10 benefit at 40% of the material cost."
      }
    ]
  },
  "endGame": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Lostbelt Arc and Challenge Quests",
        "body": "Lostbelt storylines (Part 2 onward) feature significantly stronger enemies and mandatory farming gates. Challenge Quests (high-difficulty single-stage fights) provide extra rewards for clearing with specific restrictions. For Challenge Quest preparation: always identify the buff restriction (no NP, no healing, attack debuff), build a team specifically around the restriction, and use a Support Servant from your friend list that counters the primary enemy mechanic. Farming 150 million QP for the Lostbelt Chapter ascension materials requires efficient Babel Tower farming loops."
      }
    ]
  },
  "mistakes": {
    "en": [
      "Pulling gacha on non-Limited banners—standard banners (Summoning Campaigns with existing Servants) have much lower rarity rates than Limited Event banners; save all quartz for Limited banners featuring new Servants.",
      "Ignoring Skill Materials—skill upgrade materials have different farming nodes than ascension materials; check which nodes drop your needed skill material and include that farming target in your daily AP plan.",
      "Levelling all Servants equally—it is better to have 3 Servants at max level than 10 Servants at half level; a fully levelled top-tier Servant clears content the same 10-Servant roster cannot.",
      "Spending Mana Prisms on anything other than Servant-upgrade materials—Mana Prisms are a scarce universal currency; the permanent shop items (Crystallized Lore, rare upgrade materials) provide the highest long-term value.",
      "Missing Daily Login bonuses—FGO provides escalating daily login rewards during event periods; missing 3+ consecutive days during an event period forfeits the highest-value login rewards that reset daily."
    ],
    "ja": [
      "非限定バナーでガチャを引く。標準バナー（既存サーヴァントのサモンキャンペーン）は限定イベントバナーよりレアリティ率がかなり低い。新しいサーヴァントを特集した限定バナーのために全ての聖晶石を貯める。",
